## 2. The Core Data Structure

### 2.1 Node representation

Each node stores a key, a value, and two indices (`prev`, `next`) into the arena. We use `Option<usize>` for links so the head/tail can be represented as `None`.

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::hash::Hash;

struct Node<K, V> {
    key: K,
    value: V,
    prev: Option<usize>,
    next: Option<usize>,
}
