This tutorial walks through implementing a production-quality LRU (Least Recently Used) cache in Rust from scratch. We'll cover the generic data structure, all methods, error handling, unit tests, memory-safety reasoning, concurrency options, complexity analysis, and worked examples. By the end, you'll have a complete, tested implementation you can drop into any project.

